<title>FRANCE: French sugar consumption rose in January - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French sugar consumption rose in January - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption rose to a provisional 150,000 tonnes in January from a revised 134,600 tonnes in December, French sugar intervention board FIRS said.</p>
<p>But consumption declined from 156,911 tonnes in January</p>
</text>
